-## 9. Code Examples (libcurl, POSIX)
+## 9. Rate Limiting
+
+EduGate applies a global per-client-IP rate limit before routing or request
+validation. Configure it in `config/gateway.conf` and rebuild the gateway.
+
+```c
+static const gateway_conf_t G_GATEWAY_CONF = {
+    .rate_limit_enabled        = true,
+    .rate_limit_requests       = 100,
+    .rate_limit_window_seconds = 60
+};
+```
+
+| Key | Type | Description |
+|-----|------|-------------|
+| `rate_limit_enabled` | `true`/`false` | Enables or disables gateway-wide rate limiting. |
+| `rate_limit_requests` | integer | Maximum number of requests allowed per client IP in one window. |
+| `rate_limit_window_seconds` | integer | Length of the rolling request window in seconds. |
+
+When the limit is exceeded, the gateway returns **429 Too Many Requests** with a
+JSON error body. The HTTP handler also emits a `Retry-After` header matching
+`rate_limit_window_seconds`.
+
+---
